    "# Level 1 — Required Core\n",
    "\n",
    "# Part 1: From One Neuron to a Multilayer Network\n",
    "\n",
    "A hidden unit first forms a weighted sum:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "z_k=w_{k0}+\\sum_{j=1}^{p}w_{kj}X_j,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "then applies an activation function:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A_k=g(z_k).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "ReLU is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$g(z)=\\max(0,z).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "A multilayer network feeds the activations from one layer into the next. Each hidden layer therefore creates a new representation. The output layer converts the final representation into a class score or probability.\n",
    "\n",
    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/theory.png\" alt=\"Theory\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Theory: Learning the Weights\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Forward propagation** computes predictions from current weights.\n",
    "2. A **loss function** measures prediction error.\n",
    "3. **Backpropagation** applies the chain rule to calculate gradients.\n",
    "4. An optimizer updates weights in a direction intended to reduce loss.\n",
    "\n",
    "The learning rate controls update size. A value that is too small can learn slowly; one that is too large can oscillate or fail to settle.\n"
   ]
  },
