    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/claude_task.png\" alt=\"Claude Task\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Claude Coding Task 9: Build a Tiny Scaled-Attention Demonstration\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Act as a careful deep-learning tutor.\n",
    "\n",
    "Write one NumPy-only Jupyter code cell that:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. defines four token labels and a fixed 4-by-3 matrix X;\n",
    "2. defines fixed 3-by-2 matrices W_Q, W_K, and W_V;\n",
    "3. calculates Q, K, V, scaled attention scores, row-wise softmax weights,\n",
    "   and the attention output;\n",
    "4. creates a causal mask that prevents each row from attending to later rows;\n",
    "5. prints labeled score, weight, and output tables rounded to three decimals;\n",
    "6. verifies that every attention-weight row sums to one;\n",
    "7. changes no learned weights and trains no language model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Return only the Python code.\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### <img src=\"tutorial-icons/your_workspace.png\" alt=\"Your Workspace\" width=\"30\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:8px;\"> Your Workspace\n",
    "\n",
    "Paste, read, and run Claude's response in the next cell."
   ]
